 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Someone and something",
     "texto": [
      "**-То** usually presents someone or something as existing, even when not identified: **Кто-то звонил** («someone called»). **-Нибудь** leaves the identity open and is common in questions, requests and conditions: **Ты что-нибудь хочешь?** («Do you want something?»). The use depends on the context.",
      "These forms decline and keep the hyphen: **кто-то → кого-то**, **что-нибудь → чего-нибудь**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nobody and none",
     "texto": [
      "**Никто/ничто** usually go with **не** in the verb: **Никто не пришёл** («nobody came»), **Я ничего не знаю** («I don't know anything»). With **нет** the genitive **никого** is used: **Никого нет** («there is nobody»). They also change by case: **Я никому не сказал** («I didn't tell anyone»).",
      "**Никакой** agrees with the noun and also declines: **никакой проблемы нет** («there is no problem at all»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Oneself",
     "texto": [
      "**Себя** is the reflexive pronoun that refers back to the subject and changes according to the case: **Я вижу себя** («I see myself») / **Я думаю о себе** («I think about myself»). It has no nominative form.",
      "**Сам/сама/сами** emphasises who does something and agrees with that person: **Я сам это сделал** («I did it myself», man); **Я сама это сделала** («I did it myself», woman)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
